module

public import Silmaril.Project.Defs

/-!
# Standard problem shapes: formats and values

A **shape** is a problem over arguments that silmaril registers once (open, with no expected
status), so that a project states a fact about its own artifact by filling in a row: an
instance (`silmaril instance N := SHAPE (x := …)`, or `[[instance]]` in TOML) that fixes the
shape's arguments, and an answer of that instance. Statuses transfer along the instance edge:
a proved row is SAT evidence for the shape. The catalogue is in `docs/projects/silmaril-projects.md`.

| name | statement |
|---|---|
| `silmaril.shapes.format.parses` | `Parses F b`: the bytes `b` parse under the format `F` |
| `silmaril.shapes.format.agree` | `Agree F G a b`: `a` under `F` and `b` under `G` are one value of the data model `V` |
| `silmaril.shapes.value.satisfies` | `Satisfies X P`: the value `X` parses to a `v` with `P v` |

The type arguments (`{V : Type}`) are implicit: an instance infers them from the format or
the value. A value's own obligations `X.parses` and `X.agrees.k` are generated by
`silmaril value`; these shapes are the same statements for bytes and formats that are not
(yet) a registered value, and for a predicate given as an argument.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Silmaril.Project.Shapes

/-- **The bytes `b` parse under the format `F`.** -/
@[problem "silmaril.shapes.format.parses"
  (title := "The bytes parse under a format")]
def Parses {V : Type} (F : Format blob V) (b : Silmaril.Formats.Bytes) : Prop :=
  (F.parse b).isSome = true

/-- **Two artifacts agree under the data model `V`**: `a` read under `F` and `b` read under `G`
are the same value of `V` (both parse). -/
@[problem "silmaril.shapes.format.agree"
  (title := "Two artifacts denote one value of a data model")]
def Agree {V : Type} (F G : Format blob V) (a b : Silmaril.Formats.Bytes) : Prop :=
  Equivalent F G a b

/-- **The value `X` satisfies `P`**: its bytes parse, to a value with `P`. -/
@[problem "silmaril.shapes.value.satisfies"
  (title := "A value satisfies a predicate")]
def Satisfies {V : Type} (X : Value V) (P : V → Prop) : Prop := X.Satisfies P

end Silmaril.Project.Shapes

end

